findings.body:
`build_scope` receives both lists in one positional array. It runs `shift 11`, takes `only_count` values as pathspecs (executable_revmux-round.sh:89-93), and treats everything left over as exclusions. `next` builds `scope_args` with pathspecs first, then exclusions (lines 376-383). Test 016 uses `--exclude` without `--only`. Tests 026-028 use `--only` without `--exclude`. Test 026's awk filter also drops the `Exclusions:` section before asserting.

The goal requires `--only` and `--exclude` to stay separate, and requires the tests to fail if that regresses. Several regressions would leave every test green:
- swapping the append order;
- miscounting the shift;
- copying the only values without shifting them off (`${@:1:only_count}`).

Any of these would put exclusion text into `Limited to:` and into the read commands, or list the `--only` paths under `Exclusions:`. Scale, Commits and Changed files would still look correct, because `next` computes them directly from `only_values`.
